// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-058
=adr: 058
=title: BE Agent Chat — OpenAI-Compatible Adapter
=date: 2026-04-06
=status: accepted

#ctx
~agentChat Kosmos widget exists but has no backend wiring (GAP-D2 partial)
~client owns and operates their own LLM endpoint; platform must not hardcode any vendor
~streaming token delivery required for good UX
~be_agent module gate already in licenseSlice

#opts
~a: hardcode @anthropic-ai/sdk (vendor lock-in; violates client-owned model requirement)
~b: openai npm package with configurable baseURL (de-facto standard for self-hosted + cloud LLMs)
~c: generic HTTP webhook (simpler, no streaming support)

#decision
~b: POST /api/v1/be-agent/chat gated behind be_agent module license
~openai npm package (apps/api only); baseURL=AI_CHAT_ENDPOINT; apiKey=AI_CHAT_API_KEY; model=AI_CHAT_MODEL
~stub mode: AI_CHAT_ENDPOINT unset → simulated streaming response (no crash, no external call)
~streaming: openai SSE stream → relay chunks via Socket.io be-agent:token events → agentChat widget
~system prompt context: deviceId + latest derived state + 3 recent alarms (injected per request)
~no chat history Phase 1 (stateless); history model deferred to Phase 2
~config: AI_CHAT_ENDPOINT/KEY/MODEL env vars; admin can override via SystemConfig record

#consequences
~+openai npm dep in apps/api (not web)
~+3 env vars: AI_CHAT_ENDPOINT, AI_CHAT_API_KEY, AI_CHAT_MODEL
~compatible with: Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio, Azure OpenAI, Groq, OpenRouter, any OpenAI-compat endpoint
~BeAgentService added as 23rd service; /be-agent route file added to server.ts
~no DB schema changes Phase 1

#scope
~arch_summary_update: yes
